cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, its data or its methodology, please cite it
  as shown below.
type: software
title: "PQC-Gateway: hybrid classical post-quantum TLS 1.3 gateway with benchmarking and DevSecOps"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/acostacrypto/pqc-gateway"
abstract: >-
  Prototype of a TLS 1.3 gateway negotiating the X25519MLKEM768 hybrid group
  (X25519 + ML-KEM-768) on OpenSSL 3 with oqs-provider, together with a
  reproducible benchmarking harness for handshake overhead and a DevSecOps
  pipeline (SBOM, artifact signing, vulnerability and secret scanning).
  Local, educational experimental study; not intended for production.
keywords:
  - "post-quantum cryptography"
  - "TLS 1.3"
  - "ML-KEM"
  - "hybrid key exchange"
  - "DevSecOps"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "benchmarking"
authors:
  - family-names: "Acosta Fonseca"
    given-names: "Frank Ernesto"
